NAME
       xfs_repair - check and repair a damaged XFS file system

SYNOPSIS
       xfs_repair [-n] [-L] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       xfs_repair checks an XFS file system and repairs what it finds, going
       through numbered phases. The file system must be unmounted. Unlike
       ext4, XFS is never checked at boot by fsck: when an XFS file system is
       damaged, the boot stops and you run xfs_repair from the emergency
       shell.

       Files found without a directory entry are put in lost+found.

OPTIONS
       -n     Check only; change nothing and report what would be repaired.

       -L     Clear the log first. Use it only when xfs_repair refuses
              because the log holds changes and mounting the file system (which
              would replay them) fails: those changes are lost.

EXAMPLES
           umount /mnt/data
           xfs_repair -n /dev/vgdata/lvdata
           xfs_repair /dev/vgdata/lvdata

SEE ALSO
       xfs_info(8), fsck(8), mount(8)
